    "description": "Held on 27 February 1999, the first election of the Fourth Republic after sixteen years of military rule, and run by the military-appointed transition government of General Abdulsalami Abubakar. The PDP's Olusegun Obasanjo — himself a former military head of state (1976–79) — defeated the AD–APP alliance candidate Olu Falae by 62.8% to 37.2%, carrying 27 states plus the FCT. Falae's support was concentrated in the South-West, which he swept."
